<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bziyuqo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bziyuqo was fought in 1796 in western Circassia between the commoners of the Shapsug and Natukhaj tribes and an alliance of Circassian nobles, including the princes of the Bzhedugh. The commoners won, which confirmed the end of aristocratic rule among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapsugs">Shapsugs</a> and Natukhaj. They then governed themselves through assemblies of free men, while the Bzhedugh kept their princely system.</p></div>
